1
00:00:01,000 --> 00:00:03,200
[door chime]

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:06,400
MAYA: Morning! You look like
something the cat dragged in.

3
00:00:06,900 --> 00:00:09,800
THEO: I pulled an all-nighter
fixing the oven. Again.

4
00:00:10,300 --> 00:00:13,500
- Did it work?
- Define "work".

5
00:00:14,000 --> 00:00:17,600
MAYA: So we're back to square one.
<i>Fantastic.</i>

6
00:00:18,200 --> 00:00:21,400
THEO: Hey, I'm not throwing in the towel
just yet.

7
00:00:22,000 --> 00:00:25,300
MAYA: The inspector comes at noon.
No pressure.

8
00:00:25,800 --> 00:00:28,900
THEO: Relax. I've got it covered.
Mostly.

9
00:00:29,400 --> 00:00:31,000
(oven beeping)

10
00:00:31,500 --> 00:00:34,600
MAYA: That beep is not
a good sign, is it?

11
00:00:35,100 --> 00:00:38,700
THEO: It's fine. It's just
letting off a little steam.

12
00:00:39,200 --> 00:00:42,800
MAYA: Like you after
the Henderson order?

13
00:00:43,300 --> 00:00:46,500
THEO: We agreed never
to speak of the Henderson order.

14
00:00:47,000 --> 00:00:50,600
MAYA: Fine. But if this goes south,
you're breaking the news to Gran.

15
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:53,000
♪ radio playing softly ♪

16
00:00:53,500 --> 00:00:57,000
THEO: Gran loves me.
I'm her favourite grandson.

17
00:00:57,500 --> 00:01:00,400
MAYA: You're her only grandson.
Low bar.

18
00:01:00,900 --> 00:01:04,600
THEO: A bar is a bar.
I cleared it &amp; I'm proud.

19
00:01:05,100 --> 00:01:08,900
MAYA: Okay, hotshot. Let's see
if the croissants rise to the occasion.

20
00:01:09,400 --> 00:01:12,200
[timer dings]

21
00:01:12,700 --> 00:01:16,500
THEO: Look at that. Golden.
I'm basically a genius.

22
00:01:17,000 --> 00:01:20,600
MAYA: Don't count your croissants
before they're plated.

23
00:01:21,100 --> 00:01:24,800
THEO: Is that an actual saying,
or did you just make it up?

24
00:01:25,300 --> 00:01:28,700
MAYA: I'm a baker. I knead
to have my own sayings.

25
00:01:29,200 --> 00:01:32,600
THEO: Wow. That pun was
half-baked at best.

26
00:01:33,100 --> 00:01:36,900
MAYA: And yet here you are,
eating it up.
27
00:01:37,400 --> 00:01:40,800
THEO: Fair enough. Noon, then.
We've got this.

28
00:01:41,300 --> 00:01:44,600
MAYA: We'd better. Gran's watching
from upstairs, you know.

29
00:01:45,100 --> 00:01:48,000
- She's always watching.
- Always.
